    "en": "Department of Homeland Security",
    "zh_suggested": "国土安全部"
   }
  ],
  "final_id": "022",
  "title_cn": "由纳税人资助的、支持特朗普的广告被勒令停止播出",
  "dek_cn": null,
  "body_cn": "一位联邦法官下令，特朗普政府必须停止播放任何进一步的、由纳税人资助的、宣传总统的电视广告，理由是这些广告很可能违反法律。\n\n纽约美国地区法院法官珍妮弗·罗尚于周日晚间发布了一份四页长的命令，禁止该政府使用政府资金来投放这些广告。\n\n这位法官是拜登政府任命的，她在命令中表示，必须取消“任何已安排、预订或计划用于播放或传播这些争议广告的时间段、位置或安排”。\n\n该命令立即适用于周日晚些时候计划播放的任何广告，但目前尚不清楚该裁决是否阻止了其他广告的播放。\n\n白宫未对相关评论请求做出回应。\n\n美国司法部在一份周末提交的文件中表示，这些广告的投放计划原定于周日结束。\n\n这些广告主要宣传总统及其政府的政策，并于九月份开始在全国电视台播放。这些广告的费用由国土安全部的联邦资金支付。\n\n《华尔街日报》报道称，特朗普总统亲自推动了这些广告的制作，并参与了广告的创作。\n\n该法官的裁决是对原告提起的诉讼的回应，原告包括倡导组织Common Cause（倡导组织）以及一位在阿拉巴马州竞选公职的民主党候选人。\n\n他们认为，这些支出被用于未经国会授权的目的，并违反了关于使用公共资金进行政治宣传的限制。原告在回应裁决时表示：“总统利用政府的运作机制以及国会为其他用途拨出的资金来影响选举结果，以推进其个人议程，这在法律上没有任何依据，也没有任何先例。”\n\n上周，总统表示，他计划使用其超级政治行动委员会 MAGA Inc. 的资金来支付这些备受争议的广告费用，而不是使用联邦政府的资金。",
  "context_cn": null,
  "context_attr": null
 },
 {
  "id": "E1-023",
  "page": "A3",
  "section": "U.S. News",
  "title": "DOJ Probes Networks on Halting Coverage",
  "dek": null,
  "byline": "BY JOE FLINT AND DAVE MICHAELS",
  "body_en": "The Justice Department is investigating whether major TV networks violated federal antitrust laws when they briefly suspended a rotation of broadcast journalists covering the White House last month following CNN's removal from a planned assignment.\n\nNetworks learned of the probe Friday, with Justice Department officials seeking records of communication among them regarding the pool, people familiar with the matter said.\n\nFox News, ABC News, CBS News, CNN and NBC News are part of a group of reporters, videographers, photographers and technicians who cover President Trump when he travels or when events take place in spaces that are too small for the entire press corps.\n\nWhen CNN was taken out of the rotation for Trump's trip to New York for the United Nations General Assembly in September—days after Trump banned the network, MS NOW and Politico from the White House—the TV pool briefly halted some coverage of the president.\n\n\"Members of the television press pool have boycotted covering White House events.\"\n\n\"Group boycotts among commercial competitors can violate the Sherman Act,\" Justice Department spokeswoman Emily Covington said. \"The Antitrust Division is simply investigating to determine whether these news organizations have violated the antitrust laws.\"\n\nThe White House didn't respond to a request for comment.\n\nThe Justice Department's investigation further escalates tensions between the Trump administration and the media. Trump said in July that ABC and NBC should lose their broadcast licenses for not carrying his speech on alleged election fraud on their networks.\n\nHe has also called unfavorable coverage treasonous, and his administration has subpoenaed journalists and limited access to government spaces.\n\n\"Summoning antitrust authority, on top of the retaliatory actions the White House has already taken to bar certain outlets, is another and even more brazen attempt to try to intimidate journalists,\" said Bruce Brown, president of the Reporters Committee for Freedom of the Press.\n\nFox News parent Fox Corp. and Wall Street Journal parent News Corp share common ownership.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "type": "article",
  "turn_to": null,
