 {
  "id": "E1-038",
  "page": "A8",
  "section": "World News",
  "title": "Villages Evacuated Amid Flash Flood",
  "dek": "NEPAL",
  "byline": "—Associated Press",
  "body_en": "Residents along the Budhi Gandaki river in north central Nepal evacuated Sunday as flash flooding destroyed homes and other structures in the area.\n\nThe National Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Authority evacuated villagers and warned others to move to safer areas while remaining on alert until late Sunday.\n\nThe agency said at least five people are reported missing. The flood also damaged or destroyed four bridges, swept away about three dozen houses and damaged the construction site of a hydropower plant. Several power and communication towers were also damaged along the riverside.\n\nNepal's army was continuing to rescue stranded people using helicopters and ground troops. They had rescued 49 people by Sunday afternoon.\n\nThe agency said the flash flood was caused by a landslide that blocked the Budhi Gandaki river near the village of Chumchure. The dam formed by the landslide breached, triggering the flood.\n\nThe Budhi Gandaki river merges into the Trishuli river and is a key waterway near the capital Kathmandu.",
  "priority": "P3",
  "type": "brief",
  "turn_to": null,
  "terms": [
   {
    "en": "Budhi Gandaki",
    "zh_suggested": "布迪甘达基河",
    "note": "待查"
   },
   {
    "en": "Chumchure",
    "zh_suggested": "Chumchure（村庄）",
    "note": "待查"
   }
  ],
  "final_id": "038",
  "title_cn": "突发洪水来袭，多处村庄被迫疏散。",
  "dek_cn": "尼泊尔",
  "body_cn": "尼泊尔中北部沿布迪甘达基河的居民于周日撤离，原因是突发洪水摧毁了该地区的房屋和其他建筑物。\n\n国家灾害风险降低与管理部门疏散了村民，并警告其他人转移到安全区域，同时保持警惕，直至周日晚些时候。\n\n该部门表示，至少有五人失踪。洪水还损坏或摧毁了四座桥梁，冲走了大约三十多栋房屋，并损坏了一座水电站的建设工地。沿河岸的几座电力和通信塔也遭到损坏。\n\n尼泊尔军队继续使用直升机和地面部队营救被困人员。截至周日下午，他们已营救出 49 人。\n\n该部门表示，此次突发洪水是由一场山体滑坡造成的，该滑坡堵塞了靠近 Chumchure（村庄）的布迪甘达基河。滑坡形成的堰塞坝决堤，引发了洪水。\n\n布迪甘达基河汇入特里苏利河，是首都加德满都附近的一条重要水道。",
  "context_cn": null,
  "context_attr": "无"
 },
 {
  "id": "E1-039",
  "page": "A8",
  "section": "World News",
  "title": "Arrest Made in Plot To Attack Tusk",
  "dek": "POLAND",
  "byline": "—Associated Press",
  "body_en": "A man suspected of threatening and planning to attack Polish Prime Minister Donald Tusk was arrested, the country's interior minister said Sunday.\n\nInterior Minister Marcin Kierwiński gave no details about the identity of the man nor the type of attack planned.\n\nPoland has been on high alert following a recent series of school stabbings, as well as fears of a possible Russian hybrid attack to weaken Western support for Ukraine in its war against Moscow's full-scale invasion.\n\n\"The man who threatened an attack was detained,\" Tusk wrote on X. \"Thanks to the police for fast and decisive action.\"\n\nPoland's police had said earlier on Sunday they received information about a possible plot to attack Tusk and Defense Minister Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz.\n\n\"We take this matter extremely seriously,\" said Jacek Dobrzyński, spokesperson for the minister overseeing Poland's intelligence services. He said authorities considered there was a \"high probability\" the threats would be carried out.",
  "priority": "P3",
  "type": "brief",
  "turn_to": null,
  "terms": [
   {
    "en": "Donald Tusk",
    "zh_suggested": "唐纳德·图斯克",
    "note": "波兰总理"
   },
   {
    "en": "Marcin Kierwiński",
    "zh_suggested": "马尔钦·基尔温斯基",
    "note": "波兰内政部长，待查"
   },
   {
    "en": "Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz",
    "zh_suggested": "瓦迪斯瓦夫·科西尼亚克-卡梅什",
    "note": "波兰国防部长，待查"
   },
   {
    "en": "Jacek Dobrzyński",
    "zh_suggested": "亚采克·多布任斯基",
    "note": "待查"
   }
  ],
  "final_id": "039",
  "title_cn": "警方逮捕了一名参与策划袭击唐纳德·图斯克的嫌疑人。",
  "dek_cn": "波兰",
  "body_cn": "据该国内政部长周日表示，一名涉嫌威胁并计划袭击波兰总理唐纳德·图斯克的男子已被逮捕。\n\n内政部长马尔钦·基尔温斯基没有透露该男子的身份信息，也没有说明他计划采取何种袭击方式。\n\n波兰近期发生了一系列校园持刀伤人事件，加上担心俄罗斯可能发动混合战争、削弱西方对乌克兰抵抗莫斯科全面入侵的支持，波兰已进入高度戒备状态。\n\n唐纳德·图斯克在 X 平台上写道：“威胁进行袭击的男子已被拘留。感谢警方迅速果断地采取行动。”\n\n波兰警方此前在周日表示，他们收到消息，称可能存在针对唐纳德·图斯克和国防部长瓦迪斯瓦夫·科西尼亚克-卡梅什的袭击阴谋。\n\n负责监督波兰情报事务的部长的发言人亚采克·多布任斯基表示：“我们非常重视此事。”他表示，当局认为这些威胁“很可能”会付诸行动。",
  "context_cn": null,
  "context_attr": "无"
 },
