  "title": "The WSJ Daily Crossword (Final Count, by Zhouqin Burnikel; edited by Mike Shenk)",
  "dek": null,
  "byline": null,
  "body_en": "The WSJ Daily Crossword | Edited by Mike Shenk. FINAL COUNT | By Zhouqin Burnikel.\n\nAcross: 1 Color of an igloo; 6 Foot division; 10 Plumbing piece; 14 Stand for an artist; 15 Revolutionary hero Nathan; 16 In the center of; 17 Neither gains nor loses money; 19 Nutmeg State school; 20 Blueprint detail; 21 Sandwich spread, familiarly; 22 Pale from fright; 23 Tech line caller; 25 Censorship-fighting org. since 1920; 26 Traveled hobo-style; 32 Wood for a model plane; 33 Run out of battery; 34 Fruit in a gift basket; 35 TV spots; 36 Station with shells; 40 Sch. in Tallahassee; 41 Honey bunch?; 43 Worn-down pencil; 44 Make overjoyed; 46 “Marty” Oscar winner; 50 New Mexico art town; 51 Teeny bit; 52 Cries like an infant; 54 Rum-soaked cake; 56 Analogy words; 60 Lake bordering Ontario; 61 Tune in just to complain; 63 Service bell sound; 64 Big brand in skin care; 65 Showing sulkiness; 66 Bratty attitude; 67 Motion of the ocean; 68 Take, as neighboring territory.\n\nDown: 1 Fly catchers, of a sort; 2 Instrument on a Guinness bottle; 3 “That clears things up”; 4 Saucer toppers; 5 State animal of Utah; 6 “Rumor has it...”; 7 Blue hue; 8 Jazz singer Laine; 9 Free-range fowl; 10 Record of wages; 11 “Really love your work!”; 12 Heap; 13 Garden in Genesis; 18 Captain Hook's helper; 22 Top card in a suit; 24 Minor quarrel; 25 Region; 26 Bill of HBO's “Barry”; 27 Small pair in “Full House”?; 28 Marinade in Filipino cuisine; 29 Little lie; 30 Excessive hurry; 31 “Can't argue with that!”; 32 Sheep-herding pig of film; 37 Crawlers in long lines; 38 Young panda; 39 Landlord's collection; 42 Steadiness on a ship; 45 Intermediary; 47 “Get me out of here!”; 48 Marbled steak cut; 49 Hockey score; 52 Some kings and queens; 53 Solo for a diva; 54 Indonesian island known for terraced rice fields; 55 Slightly speechless; 57 Leave; 58 Head, to Henri; 59 Stone found in cameos; 61 Fresh from the oven; 62 Craft brew, for short.\n\nPrevious Puzzle's Solution (grid): A L L I N / C O P E / E M M A; S E E N O / E R I C / G A I T; E M E R Y C L O T H / O N T V; A S S U C H / O C T E T; S E A L S / E A R; D O H / F A I R Y R I N G S; B O L / E T N A / S P I R E; A V I D / S I N K S / S C A N; N E V I L / N E I L / K I T; C R A Z Y H O R S E / G S N; Z O O / S H A D Y; G W Y N N / Z O M B I E; S I R I / S P A D E P R E S S; G L E N / H I D E / E A T I T; T A N G / U C S F / S T A N D.\n\nContest note: The contest answer is LONG. Removing the letters from both ends of each five-letter word of each theme answer yields a new six-letter word: EMERY CLOTH > merlot, FAIRY RINGS > airing, CRAZY HORSE > razors, SPADE PRESS > Padres. Those words start clues for other grid answers (LEES, ON TV, NICKS, GWYNN), and the first letters of those answers spell the contest answer.\n\n▶ Solve this puzzle online and discuss it at WSJ.com/Puzzles.",
