  "dek": "Trading by 'insiders' of a corporation, such as a company's CEO, vice president or director, potentially conveys new information about the prospects of a company. Insiders are required to report large trades to the SEC within two business days. Here's a look at the biggest individual trades by insiders, based on data received by LSEG Data and Analytics on October 9, and year-to-date stock performance of the company. Based on reports filed with regulators this past week.",
  "byline": null,
  "body_en": "KEY: B: beneficial owner of more than 10% of a security class; CB: chairman; CEO: chief executive officer; CFO: chief financial officer; CO: chief operating officer; D: director; DO: director and beneficial owner; GC: general counsel; H: officer, director and beneficial owner; I: indirect transaction filed through a trust, insider spouse, minor child or other; O: officer; OD: officer and director; unknown VP: vice president. Excludes pure options transactions. * Half the transactions were indirect. **Two day transaction. p - Pink Sheets.\n\nDate(s) | Company | Symbol | Insider | Title | No. of shrs in trans (000s) | Price range ($) in transaction | $ Value (000s) | Close ($) | Ytd (%)\n\nBuyers\nSept. 17-25 | 51Talk Online Education Group | COE | J. Huang | CEOI | 2,812 | 11.48-11.50 | 32,334 | 12.22 | -61.7\nSept. 28 | ADARx Pharmaceuticals | ADRX | S. George | DOI | 1,600 | 17.00 | 27,200 | 17.78 | (cut off)\nSept. 28 | | | C. Gordon | DOI | 950 | 17.00 | 16,150 | | \nSept. 28 | | | E. Chimovits | DI | 62 | 17.00 | 1,046 | | \nOct. 2 | GameStop | GME | R. Cohen | CEO | 700 | 24.41 | 17,084 | 26.56 | 32.3\nOct. 6 | Borr Drilling | BORR | T. Troim | DI | 1,500 | 4.24 | 6,364 | 4.78 | 18.6\nOct. 5 | | | T. Troim | DI | 1,500 | 4.13 | 6,197 | | \nOct. 7 | | | T. Troim | DI | 1,250 | 4.31 | 5,390 | | \nOct. 1 | Accelevation Holdings | ACCV | M. Rubiera | CEO | 203* | 18.00 | 3,658 | 16.72 | n.a.\nSept. 30 | Nayax | NYAX | Y. Nechmad | CEO | 44 | 46.39-48.56 | 2,112 | 45.60 | -9.9\nOct. 5 | Sonic Automotive | SAH | P. Rusnak | B | 28 | 59.76 | 1,659 | 60.56 | -2.1\nOct. 1 | | | P. Rusnak | B | 22 | 59.50 | 1,288 | | \nSept. 28 | Pampa Energia | PAM | D. Mindlin | O | 15 | 77.63 | 1,164 | 80.34 | -9.2\nOct. 1-2 | Outset Medical | OM | B. Leonard | BI | 245 | 3.53-3.88 | 870 | 4.05 | 9.2\nOct. 2 | Prothena | PRTA | W. Scully | BI | 100 | 8.57 | 857 | 8.84 | -7.4\nSept. 30 | First Guaranty Bancshares | FGBI | E. Smith | DOI | 99 | 8.28 | 822 | 8.34 | 55.3\nOct. 7 | H.B. Fuller | FUL | R. Bailly | DI | 10 | 50.00 | 500 | 49.56 | -16.6\nOct. 7 | Immersion | IMMR | E. Singer | CEO | 41 | 7.11-7.15 | 293 | 7.43 | 9.3\n\nSellers\nOct. 5 | Elastic | ESTC | S. Schuurman | DI | 1,500 | 90.13 | 135,195 | 98.23 | 30.2\nOct. 5 | Nebius Group | NBIS | O. Nave | CO | 500 | 231.12-243.50 | 117,765 | 221.07 | 164.1\nOct. 6 | Arista Networks | ANET | J. Ullal | CEOI | 460 | 211.36-213.06 | 97,643 | 216.74 | 65.4\nSept. 30 | CrowdStrike Holdings | CRWD | M. Sentonas | P | 242 | 262.71-267.96 | 64,225 | 275.04 | 134.7\nOct. 1 | | | S. Gandhi | DI | 54 | 260.34-269.07 | 14,322 | | \nOct. 2 | Apple | AAPL | T. Cook | OD | 192 | 331.44-333.94 | 63,846 | 336.64 | 23.8\nOct. 2 | | | D. O'Brien | O | 46 | 333.35-333.91 | 15,467 | | \nOct. 5 | Robinhood Markets | HOOD | V. Tenev | CEO | 375 | 113.24-114.95 | 42,644 | 109.02 | -3.6\nOct. 5-7 | Cloudflare | NET | M. Zatlyn | CBI | 99 | 346.40-369.34 | 35,236 | 360.93 | 83.1\nOct. 6-7 | Nutanix | NTNX | R. Ramaswami | CEO | 400 | 73.35-74.00 | 29,460 | 74.63 | 44.4\nOct. 1 | Lumentum Holdings | LITE | W. Ali | CFO | 25 | 1048.50 | 25,732 | 1103.36 | 199.3\nOct. 6 | Trane Technologies | TT | D. Regnery | CEO | 48 | 480.00 | 23,084 | 476.98 | 22.6\nOct. 5-6 | Gap | GAP | W. Fisher | DO | 934 | 23.35-23.89 | 22,071 | 23.23 | -9.3\nOct. 6 | Workday | WDAY | D. Duffield | BI | 99 | 184.80-189.39 | 18,587 | 186.59 | -13.1\nOct. 1 | | | D. Duffield | BI | 98 | 183.86-194.77 | 18,416 | | \nOct. 2 | Snowflake | SNOW | M. Speiser | D | 51* | 344.00 | 17,455 | 368.89 | 68.2\nOct. 7 | | | B. Dageville | DI | 50 | 333.42 | 16,671 | | \nOct. 1 | Seagate Technology Holdings | STX | W. Mosley | CEO | 19 | 898.10-927.90 | 17,377 | 783.00 | 184.3",
