 {
  "id": "E3-032",
  "page": "B7",
  "section": "Heard on the Street",
  "title": "Home Builders and Sellers Vie for Buyers",
  "dek": "Competition is heating up, which will force companies like Lennar and KB Home to beef up incentives",
  "byline": null,
  "body_en": "Ready to be realistic about the value of your home now that mortgage rates are above 7%? Builders won't thank you for it.\n\nHome builders had one thing working in their favor over the past four years: Regular home sellers weren't willing to budge on prices, so competition from the existing home market was low.\n\nThis is starting to change, which will hurt builders' already diminished profit margins.\n\nLennar and KB Home said recently that they are facing tougher competition from regular owners who are more motivated to sell. The average price Lennar sold homes for in its west region over the three months through August was $44,000 lower than the same period last year—a 7% drop. Average prices in its central region dropped 5% compared with a year ago. It said stiffer competition from the existing-home market was one factor behind the declines.\n\nKB Home lowered the midpoint of its average sales-price estimate for the fourth quarter from $500,000 to $480,000. Southern Californian home sellers are cutting their prices to entice buyers, so KB Home has to follow or risk missing out on sales.\n\nIn the four weeks through Sept. 20, 21% of sellers in the existing-home market dropped their asking price, data from Redfin shows. The most significant activity is happening with concessions, which don't show up in headline prices.\n\nIn August, 45% of home sellers gave concessions to buyers, such as offering to cover the closing costs or handing the buyer money for repairs. In oversupplied Sunbelt markets such as Atlanta and Nashville, Tenn., 7 in 10 sellers are now offering concessions. These are the same markets where home builders tend to cluster.\n\nOutright price cuts are likely to become more common because the number of homes for sale is almost back to prepandemic levels. In September, inventory was 5% below the same month of 2019, according to data from Realtor.com.\n\nThe pandemic-era housing boom sent the usual competitive dynamic between the new-home and existing-home markets haywire. Last year, sales of existing homes were one-fifth below 2022 levels.\n\nOnce mortgage rates began to rise four years ago, owners with ultralow rates stayed put, starving the for-sale market of supply. And many sellers had a \"here is my price, make me move\" mentality. They preferred to take their property off the market rather than accept a lower offer.\n\nThat suited builders nicely.\n\n[Print edition continues but is cut off in extraction after:] The downside is that the buydowns are expensive and have sapped profit margins. Lennar currently has to offer incentives such as rate buydowns worth 12% of the value of a home to get deals done. In the three months through August, the company's gross margin was 15.8%—back at levels last seen in the aftermath of the 2008-09 financial crisis. Things might get worse. Higher [text ends]\n\n[Chart: Sales incentives on newly built homes as a percentage of revenue, 2009–2026. Note: No data available for 4Q 2019 through 4Q 2020 due to Covid-19 pandemic. Source: John Burns Research & Consulting.]\n\n[Photo: David Paul Morris/Bloomberg News]",
  "priority": "P2",
  "type": "opinion",
  "turn_to": null,
  "terms": [
   {
    "en": "Lennar",
    "zh_suggested": "莱纳（美国住宅建筑商）",
    "note": null
   },
   {
    "en": "KB Home",
    "zh_suggested": "KB Home（美国住宅建筑商）",
    "note": null
   },
   {
    "en": "Redfin",
    "zh_suggested": "Redfin（房产平台）",
    "note": null
   },
   {
    "en": "Realtor.com",
    "zh_suggested": "Realtor.com（房产平台）",
    "note": null
   },
   {
    "en": "rate buydowns",
    "zh_suggested": "利率买断（卖方贴息降月供）",
    "note": null
   }
  ],
  "final_id": "111",
  "title_cn": "住宅建筑商与卖家争抢购房者",
  "dek_cn": "竞争加剧将迫使莱纳（美国住宅建筑商）、KB Home（美国住宅建筑商）等公司加大激励力度",
  "body_cn": "现在，随着抵押贷款利率超过 7%，您是否准备好对房屋的价值进行更现实的评估？建筑商可能不会因此感谢您。\n\n在过去的四年里，房屋建筑商一直受益于一个有利因素：普通房屋的出售者不愿降低价格，因此现有房屋市场的竞争压力较小。\n\n但这种情况正在发生变化，这将进一步削弱建筑商本已缩小的利润空间。\n\n莱纳和 KB Home最近表示，他们面临着来自普通房屋出售者的更强竞争，这些出售者更有动力出售房屋。莱纳在截至 8 月的三个月内，其西部地区的房屋平均售价比去年同期下降了 44,000 美元，降幅为 7%。其中部地区的平均价格比一年前下降了 5%。该公司表示，来自现有房屋市场的更强竞争是导致价格下降的一个因素。\n\nKB Home将其第四季度平均售价的预估中点从 50 万美元下调至 48 万美元。南加州地区的房屋出售者正在降低价格以吸引买家，因此 KB Home必须跟上，否则可能会错失销售机会。\n\nRedfin（房产平台）的数据显示，在截至 9 月 20 日的四周内，现有房屋市场中 21% 的出售者降低了他们的要价。最显著的变化体现在让步方面，而这些让步不会反映在标价中。\n\n8 月，45% 的房屋出售者向买家提供了让步，例如提供支付交易成本或向买家提供维修费用。在亚特兰大和田纳西州纳什维尔等供应过剩的“阳光地带”市场中，现在有 70% 的出售者提供让步。这些市场也是房屋建筑商通常聚集的地方。\n\n直接降价的情况可能会变得更加普遍，因为待售房屋的数量几乎恢复到了疫情前的水平。Realtor.com（房产平台）的数据显示，9 月份的库存量比 2019 年同期的水平低 5%。\n\n疫情期间的房地产繁荣打破了新建房屋市场和现有房屋市场之间通常的竞争动态。去年，现有房屋的销售量比 2022 年的水平下降了五分之一。\n\n四年前，抵押贷款利率开始上升后，那些拥有超低利率的房主选择继续持有房屋，导致待售房屋的供应量减少。而且，许多出售者都抱着“这是我的价格，如果你们想买，就出这个价”的心态。他们宁愿将房屋从市场上撤下，也不愿接受较低的报价。\n\n这对建筑商来说非常有利。\n\n[印刷版继续，但在提取内容中被截断：] 缺点是，这种“利率买断”方式成本高昂，并降低了利润空间。莱纳目前必须提供诸如“利率买断”之类的激励措施，其价值相当于房屋价值的 12%，才能促成交易。在截至 8 月的三个月里，该公司的毛利率为 15.8%，回到了 2008-09 年金融危机之后的水准。情况可能会变得更糟。更高的[文本结束]\n\n[图表：新建房屋销售激励措施占收入的百分比，2009-2026 年。注：由于新冠疫情，2019 年第四季度至 2020 年第四季度的数据不可用。来源：John Burns Research & Consulting。]\n\n[照片：David Paul Morris/彭博新闻社]",
  "context_cn": null,
  "context_attr": null
 },
 {
  "id": "E3-033",
  "page": "B7",
  "section": "Money & Investing",
  "title": "Stock Spotlight",
  "dek": null,
  "byline": null,
  "body_en": "Space Exploration Technologies: Shares climbed 1.2% after the company struck a deal for cellular spectrum licenses in a big play to become a wireless carrier.\n\nDelta Air Lines: Shares in the carrier ended the day roughly flat, making up early losses after Delta cut its earnings outlook following another quarter of persistently high fuel costs.\n\nHumana: The health insurer surged 12% after the U.S. government improved its rating for the company's Medicare Advantage plans, putting it in line for more bonus payments.\n\nApple: Shares fell 1.1%, after Nikkei Asia reported the company told some of its suppliers to cut production of parts for its new iPhone 18 lineup because of softer demand.\n\nAvient: Shares of the materials solutions provider fell 7.8% after the company said Ashish Khandpur had stepped down as chief executive officer.",
  "priority": "P3",
  "type": "brief",
  "turn_to": null,
  "terms": [
   {
    "en": "Space Exploration Technologies (SpaceX)",
    "zh_suggested": "SpaceX",
    "note": "收购蜂窝频谱牌照，进军无线运营商"
   },
   {
    "en": "Humana",
    "zh_suggested": "Humana（美国健康保险商）",
    "note": "Medicare Advantage评级上调，涨12%"
   },
   {
    "en": "Avient",
    "zh_suggested": "Avient（材料方案商）",
    "note": "CEO Ashish Khandpur卸任，跌7.8%"
   },
   {
    "en": "iPhone 18",
    "zh_suggested": "iPhone 18",
    "note": "日经称苹果因需求疲软砍单"
   }
  ],
  "final_id": "112",
  "title_cn": "值得关注的股票",
  "dek_cn": null,
  "body_cn": "SpaceX：该公司达成了一项协议，获得了蜂窝频谱许可，旨在成为一家无线运营商，消息公布后，其股价上涨了1.2%。\n\n达美航空：该航空公司的股价在当天收盘时基本保持平稳，弥补了早盘的跌幅，此前达美航空在连续一个季度面临持续高昂的燃油成本后，下调了其盈利预期。\n\nHumana（美国健康保险商）：美国政府提高了该公司医疗保险优势计划的评级后，Humana的股价飙升了12%，使其有望获得更多奖金。\n\n苹果公司：在《日经亚洲》报道称，由于需求疲软，该公司已告知部分供应商减少其新款iPhone 18系列产品的零部件生产后，苹果公司的股价下跌了1.1%。\n\nAvient（材料方案商）：该公司表示，阿希什·坎德普尔已卸任首席执行官一职后，该材料解决方案供应商的股价下跌了7.8%。",
  "context_cn": null,
  "context_attr": null
 },
 {
  "id": "E3-034",
  "page": "B7",
  "section": "Money & Investing",
  "title": "Investors' No. 1 Worry",
  "dek": null,
  "byline": "By Cristina Roca",
  "body_en": "Investors were rattled by contagion fears over a bond-market meltdown in France.\n\nBut when it comes to risks looming over the market next year, they have bigger things to worry about—at least according to George Saravelos, head of foreign-exchange research at Deutsche Bank, who summarized his conversations with clients this week like this:\n\n\"The biggest systemic risk in the market next year is not France but 'something going wrong' in the AI ecosystem: a safety event, a failed IPO, or disappointing revenues.\"\n\nSaravelos cited a Brookings paper that recently estimated AI labs need to generate upward of $3.5 trillion a year by 2032 to earn a return on data-center investments.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "type": "brief",
  "turn_to": null,
  "terms": [
   {
    "en": "George Saravelos",
    "zh_suggested": "乔治·萨拉维洛斯（德银外汇研究主管）",
    "note": null
   },
   {
    "en": "Brookings",
    "zh_suggested": "布鲁金斯学会",
    "note": null
   }
  ],
  "final_id": "113",
  "title_cn": "投资者的头号担忧",
  "dek_cn": null,
  "body_cn": "法国债券市场崩盘引发的连锁反应风险令投资者感到不安。\n\n但如果说明年市场面临的风险，投资者更应该关注的是其他更重要的问题——至少根据德意志银行外汇研究主管乔治·萨拉维洛斯（德银外汇研究主管）的说法，他本周总结了与客户的对话，并表示：\n\n“明年市场面临的最大系统性风险不是法国，而是人工智能生态系统中可能出现的‘问题’：例如安全事件、首次公开募股失败或营收未达预期。”\n\n萨拉维洛斯引用了一份布鲁金斯学会的研究报告，该报告最近估计，到2032年，人工智能实验室需要产生超过3.5万亿美元的年收入，才能获得数据中心投资的回报。",
  "context_cn": null,
  "context_attr": null
 },
 {
  "id": "E3-035",
  "page": "B7",
  "section": "Money & Investing",
  "title": "In Market History",
  "dek": null,
  "byline": null,
  "body_en": "On this day in 1982, after nearly 17 years of going nowhere, the Dow Jones Industrial Average finally rose above the peak it set in the bull market of the 1960s.",
  "priority": "P3",
  "type": "brief",
  "turn_to": null,
  "terms": [],
  "final_id": "114",
  "title_cn": "市场历史上的今天",
  "dek_cn": null,
  "body_cn": "1982年的这一天，在经历了近17年的停滞不前之后，道琼斯工业平均指数终于突破了其在20世纪60年代牛市中所达到的最高点。",
  "context_cn": null,
  "context_attr": null
 },
 {
  "id": "E3-036",
  "page": "B7",
  "section": "Data",
  "title": "Share-price performance: Wireless Firms' Day of Woe",
  "dek": null,
  "byline": null,
  "body_en": "Share-price performance chart (intraday, 10 a.m. to 4 p.m.): AT&T, Verizon, T-Mobile US.\n\nShares in AT&T, Verizon Communications and T-Mobile US fell sharply Friday in the wake of SpaceX's $8 billion spectrum deal. AT&T and Verizon suffered their biggest one-day declines in more than 24 years. For T-Mobile, it was the worst percentage drop in more than 13 years. AT&T closed down 9.8%, Verizon fell 8.7% and T-Mobile declined 13%.\n\nSource: FactSet.",
  "priority": "P3",
  "type": "data_table",
  "turn_to": null,
  "terms": [],
  "final_id": "115",
