  "dek": null,
  "byline": null,
  "body_en": "THE TICKER | MARKET EVENTS COMING THIS WEEK\n\nMonday\nU.S. Bond markets are closed for Columbus Day holiday.\nEarnings expected (Estimate/Year Ago): Citigroup 2.65/1.86; Goldman Sachs 12.86/12.25; Johnson & Johnson 2.50/2.80 (Johnson & Johnson is expected to post a profit of $2.50 a share); JPMorgan Chase 5.93/5.07; UnitedHealth Group 4.15/2.92; Wells Fargo 1.85/1.66; BlackRock 14.33/11.55; Fastenal 0.34/0.29; Home BancShares 0.64/0.61; Morgan Stanley 2.93/2.80; State Street 3.68/2.78; Charles Schwab 1.66/1.31; Marsh & McLennan 1.97/1.85; Bank of New York Mellon 2.27/1.88; PNC Financial Services 4.91/4.35.\n\nTuesday\nExisting home sales: Aug., previous 3.98 mil.; Sep., expected 3.95 mil.\nTreasury budget: Sep. '25, $198 bil. surplus; Sep. '26, expected n.a.\n\nWednesday\nConsumer price index: All items, Aug. up 3.4%; Sep., expected up 3.7%; Core, Aug. up 2.4%; Sep., expected up 2.5%.\nMortgage bankers indexes: Purchases, previous down 2.0%; Refinancings, previous down 8.0%.\nEmpire Manufacturing: Sep., previous 7.6; Oct., expected n.a.\nInitial jobless claims: Previous 197,000; Expected 202,000.\nPhiladelphia Fed survey: Sep., previous 37.8; Oct., expected 35.0.\n\nThursday\nBusiness inventories: Jul., previous up 0.8%; Aug., expected up 0.4%.\nEIA status report (previous change in stocks, millions of barrels): Crude-oil stocks down 3.2; Gasoline stocks up 0.4; Distillates up 0.0.\nFreddie Mac mortgage survey (previous weekly averages): 30-year fixed 7.40%; 15-year fixed 6.73%.\nProducer price index: All items, Aug. up 0.4%; Sep., expected up 0.6%.\nRetail sales: Aug., previous up 1.2%; Sep., expected up 0.4%; ex. autos, Aug. previous up 1.4%, Sep. expected up 0.6%.\nEIA report: natural-gas (previous change in stocks in billions of cubic feet).\n\n* FactSet Estimates: earnings-per-share estimates don't include extraordinary items (losses in parentheses). Adjusted for stock split. Note: Forecasts are from Dow Jones weekly survey of economists.",
